<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47672" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέτᾰ</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχέτας</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχέτᾰ</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clear-sounding, musical,
				shrill</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόναξ ἀχέτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					575
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					151
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); epith. of the cicada, <i>chirping</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέτα τέττιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					582
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.201
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pamphil.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχέτατ</span>. ib.<i><span class="en">
				213
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Arch.
			</span></i>): abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχέτας, ὁ</span>, <i>the chirper</i>, i.e. <i>the male
				cicada</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anan.
				5.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1159
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				1095
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				532b16
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				556a20
			</span></i>: <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				1250
			</span></i> has 
				Ep.
			acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέτα πορθμόν</span> the
				<i>sounding</i> strait.</div>
